\[Z_{P}=\left[\begin{array}{cc}
40 &amp; 60 \\
80 &amp; 100
\end{array}\right] ; \quad Y_{Q}=\left[\begin{array}{cc}
5 S &amp; -2.5 S \\
-2.5 S &amp; 1 S
\end{array}\right]\] <br/>
From \(Z_{p}\) matrix
<br/> \[\begin{aligned}
&amp; V_{1}=40 I_{1}+60 I_{2} \\
&amp; V_{2}=80 I_{1}+100 I_{2}
\end{aligned}\] <br/>
Convert Z-parameters in to ABCD parameters
<br/> \[\begin{aligned}
V_{1} &amp; =A V_{2}-B I_{2} \\
I_{1} &amp; =C V_{2}-D I_{2}
\end{aligned}\] <br/>
From equation (ii),
<br/> \[\begin{aligned}
&amp; I_{1}=\frac{V_{2}}{80}-\frac{100}{80} I_{2} \\
&amp; I_{1}=\frac{V_{2}}{80}-\frac{5}{4} I_{2}
\end{aligned}\] <br/>
Sub equation (iii) in equation (i),
<br/> \[\begin{aligned}
&amp; V_{1}=40\left(\frac{V_{2}}{80}-\frac{5}{4} I_{2}\right)+60 I_{2} \\
&amp; V_{1}=\frac{V_{2}}{2}+10 I_{2}
\end{aligned}\] <br/>
From equation (iii) and (iv),
<br/> \[\begin{aligned}
{\left[\begin{array}{ll}
A_{1} &amp; B_{1} \\
C_{1} &amp; D_{1}
\end{array}\right] } &amp; =\left[\begin{array}{cc}
0.5 &amp; -10 \\
\frac{1}{80} &amp; \frac{5}{4}
\end{array}\right] \\
{[Y]_{Q} } &amp; =\left[\begin{array}{cc}
5 &amp; -2.5 \\
-2.5 &amp; 1
\end{array}\right]
\end{aligned}\] <br/>
<br/> \[\begin{aligned}
&amp; I_{1}=5 V_{1}-2.5 V_{2} \\
&amp; I_{2}=-2.5 V_{1}+V_{2}
\end{aligned}\] <br/>
Convert \(Y\)-parameters to \(\mathrm{ABCD}\) parameters
From equation (vi),
<br/> \[\begin{aligned}
&amp; V_{1}=\frac{V_{2}}{2.5}-\frac{I_{2}}{2.5} \\
&amp; V_{1}=0.4 V_{2}-0.4 I_{2}
\end{aligned}\] <br/>
Sub equation (vii) in equation ( \(\mathrm{v}\) ),
<br/> \[\begin{aligned}
I_{1} &amp; =5\left(0.4 V_{2}-0.4 I_{2}\right)-2.5 V_{2} \\
&amp; =2 V_{2}-2 I_{2}-2.5 V_{2} \\
I_{1} &amp; =-0.5 V_{2}-2 I_{2}
\end{aligned}\] <br/>
From equation (vii) and equation (viii),
<br/> \[\begin{aligned}
{\left[\begin{array}{ll}
A_{2} &amp; B_{2} \\
C_{2} &amp; D_{2}
\end{array}\right] } &amp; =\left[\begin{array}{cc}
0.4 &amp; 0.4 \\
-0.5 &amp; 2
\end{array}\right] \\
T &amp; =\left[\begin{array}{ll}
A_{1} &amp; B_{1} \\
C_{1} &amp; D_{1}
\end{array}\right] *\left[\begin{array}{ll}
A_{2} &amp; B_{2} \\
C_{2} &amp; D_{2}
\end{array}\right] \\
&amp; =\left[\begin{array}{cc}
0.5 &amp; -10 \\
\frac{1}{80} &amp; \frac{5}{4}
\end{array}\right] *\left[\begin{array}{cc}
0.4 &amp; 0.4 \\
-0.5 &amp; 2
\end{array}\right] \\
\beta &amp; =0.5 \times 0.4+(-10) \times 2 \\
&amp; =-19.8 \Omega
\end{aligned}\]

\[\begin{aligned}
V_{0} &amp; =\frac{V_{S}}{1-\alpha} \\
40 &amp; =\frac{20}{1-\alpha} \\
\alpha &amp; =0.5 \\
I_{0} &amp; =\frac{V_{0}}{R}=\frac{40}{10}=4 \mathrm{~A}
\end{aligned}\] <br/>
Boost :
<br/> \[\begin{aligned}
I_{L} &amp; =\frac{I_{0}}{1-\alpha}=\frac{4}{1-0.5}=8 \mathrm{~A} \\
\Delta I_{L} &amp; =\frac{\alpha V_{s}}{f C}=\frac{0.5 \times 20}{500 \times 2.10^{-3}}=10 \\
I_{m x} &amp; =(i L)_{\text {peak }} \\
&amp; =I_{L}+\frac{\Delta I_{L}}{2}=8+\frac{10}{2}=13 \mathrm{~A}
\end{aligned}\]

\[\begin{aligned}
x: y &amp; =(a+1):(a-1) \\
\frac{x}{y} &amp; =\frac{(a+1)}{(a-1)} \\
\frac{x^2-y^2}{x^2+y^2} &amp; =\frac{\left(\frac{x}{y}\right)^2-1}{\left(\frac{x}{y}\right)^2+1}
\end{aligned}\] <br/>
<br/> \[\begin{aligned}
&amp; =\frac{\left(\frac{(a+1)}{(a-1)}\right)^{2}-1}{\left(\frac{(a+1)}{(a-1)}\right)^{2}-1} \\
&amp; =\frac{(a+1)^{2}-(a-1)^{2}}{(a+1)^{2}+(a-1)^{2}} \\
&amp; =\frac{4 a}{2 a^{2}+2}=\frac{2 a}{a^{2}+1}
\end{aligned}\]
